   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Write \\( x = r\\cos\\theta \\) and \\( y = r\\sin\\theta \\), and differentiate r by the chain rule: \\( \\frac{dr}{d\\theta} = - 14 \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)} \\), which is \\( 7 \\sqrt{3} \\) at \\( \\theta = \\frac{5 \\pi}{6} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            7,
            [
               "Sqrt",
               3
            ]
         ],
         "rule_named": "chain rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the product rule, \\( \\frac{dy}{d\\theta} = \\frac{dr}{d\\theta}\\sin\\theta + r\\cos\\theta \\) and \\( \\frac{dx}{d\\theta} = \\frac{dr}{d\\theta}\\cos\\theta - r\\sin\\theta \\). At \\( \\theta = \\frac{5 \\pi}{6} \\) these are \\( \\frac{5 \\sqrt{3}}{4} \\) and \\( - \\frac{51}{4} \\).",
         "rule_named": "product rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The slope is \\( \\frac{dy/d\\theta}{dx/d\\theta} = - \\frac{5 \\sqrt{3}}{51} \\).",
